$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S)-2-[N-(N’-Benzylpropyl)amino]benzophenone hydrochloride S12. To a
stirring solution of N-methylimidazole (5.88 mL, 73.8 mmol) in anhydrous
CH2Cl2 (90 mL) at 0 °C under an atmosphere of N2, was added
methanesulfonyl chloride (1.44 mL, 18.5 mmol) followed by BP·HCl S11
(4.475 g, 18.5 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for 5 min, after
which 2-aminobenzophenone (3.29 g, 16.7 mmol) was added at room
temperature. The resultant mixture was stirred at 48 °C for 19 h, and
then quenched with saturated ammonium chloride solution (40 mL). The
aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 100 mL) and the combined
organic extracts were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was diluted with minimal
acetone, acidified with concentrated HCl to pH 2 and stirred at room
temperature for 3 h. The resulting solid was filtered, washed with ice
cold acetone and air dried. The title compound S12 as a pale cream solid
(6.47 g, 83%). [α]D 20 = -114 (c 1.00, MeOH) (lit.4 -134 c 1.00, MeOH);
1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD): δ 1.59-1.68 (1H, m, Proβ-HAHB), 1.83-1.94 (1H,
m, Proγ-HAHB), 2.11-2.21 (1H, m, Proγ-HAHB), 2.37-2.47 (1H, m,
Proβ-HAHB), 3.32-3.39 (2H, m, Proδ-HAHB), 3.56-3.61 (1H, m, Proδ-HAHB),
4.32-4.40 (3H, m, Proα-H, NCH2C), 7.40-7.80 (14H, m, Ar-H, NH); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CD3OD): δ 23.8 (CH2, Proγ-C), 29.5 (CH2, Proβ-C), 55.8 (CH2,
Proδ-C), 59.3 (CH2, NCH2C), 68.0 (CH, Proα-C), 125.6 (CH, Ar-CH), 126.9
(CH, Ar-CH), 129.5 (CH, 2 x Ar-CH), 130.2 (CH, 2 x Ar-CH), 131.1 (C,
Ar-C), 131.2 (CH, 3 x Ar-CH), 131.5 (CH, Ar-CH), 132.0 (CH, 2 x Ar-CH),
133.1 (CH, Ar-CH), 134.3 (CH, Ar-CH), 136.0 (C, Ar-C), 138.5 (C, Ar-C),
167.2 (C, CONH), 197.6 (C, C2CO).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of the Cyclic Depsipeptide YM-280193, a Platelet
Aggregation Inhibitor
